IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tprai-types`
IMPORT `tprai-transfer`
IMPORT `tprai-recovery`
IMPORT `tprai-information`

-- Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "Have the insured's rights against its insurer passed to the third party;
--    can it enforce them yet; how much can it recover from the insurer, and
--    how much of the liability can it still enforce against the insured; and
--    by when must information be given?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Third party case` HAS
    `the transfer facts`                                IS A `Transfer facts`
    `the money facts`                                   IS A `Money facts`
    `an information notice`                             IS A MAYBE `Notice facts`
    `a disclosure notice`                               IS A MAYBE `Disclosure notice facts`

DECLARE `Third party position` HAS
    `rights transferred`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `may enforce against the insurer now`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount due from the insurer`                       IS A NUMBER
    `amount still enforceable against the insured`      IS A NUMBER
    `last day to provide information`                   IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day to serve a list of documents`             IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref ss 1, 4-10, 14, 15, Sch 1, Sch 3
@export default The position under the Third Parties (Rights against Insurers) Act 2010 (UK) for a third party owed a liability by an insured: whether the insured's rights against its insurer have been transferred (ss 1, 4-7, 15, Sch 3); whether the third party may enforce them now (liability established, s 1(3)-(4)); the amount due from the insurer (ss 8, 10; 0 if nothing transferred); the amount it may still enforce against the insured (s 14; the whole liability if nothing transferred); and the last days for information (Sch 1 para 2) and a list of documents (para 4(3)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Third party case`  @desc The relevant-person event and dates, the amounts, and any notices received
GIVETH A `Third party position`
`the third party position for` c MEANS
    `Third party position` WITH
        `rights transferred`                            IS transferred
        `may enforce against the insurer now`           IS transferred AND `the third party may enforce the transferred rights under` m
        `amount due from the insurer`                   IS IF transferred THEN `the amount due from the insurer under` m ELSE 0
        `amount still enforceable against the insured`  IS
            IF transferred THEN `the amount still enforceable against the insured under` m ELSE m's `the insured's liability to the third party`
        `last day to provide information`               IS
            CONSIDER c's `an information notice`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN `the last day to provide information under` n
        `last day to serve a list of documents`         IS
            CONSIDER c's `a disclosure notice`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST n  THEN `the last day to serve a list of documents under` n
    WHERE
        m MEANS c's `the money facts`
        transferred MEANS `the rights are transferred under` (c's `the transfer facts`)
